From: 06n-arch <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:21:08 -0500
Subject: drm/panthor: Sky1: register the GPU Energy Model from SCMI

CIX's 0063 adds cix_scmi_register_em(), which builds an Energy Model for
the GPU from the SCMI perf domain's power estimates, but nothing calls
it. The devfreq cooling device is therefore registered without an EM,
and the power_allocator governor that CIX's ACPI thermal zones are
tuned for (SSTP sustainable power, SWIT switch-on trip) refuses the GPU
zone:

  thermal thermal_zone4: power_allocator: devfreq-CIXH5000:00 is not a power actor
  thermal thermal_zone4: power_allocator: binding failed

so TZGT stays on step_wise and throttles the GPU from its 70 C
switch-on trip rather than managing it against a power budget.

When DVFS goes through the SCMI perf genpd, register the EM before the
cooling device. On a Radxa Orion O6N the firmware reports 0.96 W at
72 MHz up to 10.7 W at 1 GHz, and TZGT then accepts power_allocator.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c
index 6d0778eb4..c7f0932dc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c
@@ -4,10 +4,12 @@
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/devfreq.h>
 #include <linux/devfreq_cooling.h>
+#include <linux/energy_model.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/pm_domain.h>
 #include <linux/pm_opp.h>
 #include <linux/scmi_perf_domain.h>
+#include <linux/cix/cix_scmi_em.h>
 
 #include <drm/drm_managed.h>
 #include <drm/drm_print.h>
@@ -277,6 +279,11 @@ static void panthor_devfreq_perf_dev_release(struct drm_device *ddev, void *arg)
 	}
 }
 
+static void panthor_devfreq_em_release(void *dev)
+{
+	em_dev_unregister_perf_domain(dev);
+}
+
 int panthor_devfreq_init(struct panthor_device *ptdev)
 {
 	/* There's actually 2 regulators (mali and sram), but the OPP core only
@@ -433,6 +440,22 @@ int panthor_devfreq_init(struct panthor_device *ptdev)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * With SCMI DVFS the firmware knows the GPU's power at each OPP. Give
+	 * the device an Energy Model built from it so the devfreq cooling
+	 * device is a power actor; without one the power_allocator governor
+	 * refuses to bind the GPU thermal zone.
+	 */
+	if (IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_CIX_SCMI_ENERGY_MODEL) &&
+	    pdevfreq->opp_dev && !em_pd_get(dev)) {
+		ret = cix_scmi_register_em(dev);
+		if (!ret)
+			ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, panthor_devfreq_em_release,
+						       dev);
+		if (ret)
+			DRM_DEV_INFO(dev, "No GPU Energy Model: %d\n", ret);
+	}
+
 	cooling = devfreq_cooling_em_register(pdevfreq->devfreq, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(cooling))
 		DRM_DEV_INFO(dev, "Failed to register cooling device\n");
